From: Koral Ilgun <koral.ilgun@adtran.com>
Date: Mon, 09 Nov 2026 12:12:52 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] BSS coloring: Cancel the collision timer of a BSS that is not started

hostapd_switch_color() arms the collision timer for bss[0] of an
interface, also when that BSS is not started.
hostapd_free_hapd_data() returns early for a BSS that is not started,
before it cancels the timer. So a BSS that is freed in that state
leaves the timer behind, and the timer handler then reads the freed
BSS. This happens when an interface that waits for its country update
is stopped and its BSSes are removed.

Cancel the timer at the start of hostapd_free_hapd_data(), with the
other timers that the function cancels for every BSS.

Fixes: 654d2395dddf ("BSS coloring: Handling of collision events and triggering CCA")
Signed-off-by: Koral Ilgun <koral.ilgun@adtran.com>
---
--- a/src/ap/hostapd.c
+++ b/src/ap/hostapd.c
@@ -1526,6 +1526,12 @@ void hostapd_adv_ttlm_event(struct hosta
 
 void hostapd_free_hapd_data(struct hostapd_data *hapd)
 {
+#ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211AX
+	/* A color collision event arms this timer also for a BSS that is not
+	 * started, and the BSS can be freed before the timer expires. */
+	eloop_cancel_timeout(hostapd_switch_color_timeout_handler, hapd, NULL);
+#endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211AX */
+
 #ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
 	eloop_cancel_timeout(hostapd_link_remove_timeout_handler, hapd, NULL);
 	eloop_cancel_timeout(hostapd_link_remove_finish, hapd, NULL);
@@ -1704,11 +1710,6 @@ void hostapd_free_hapd_data(struct hosta
 	}
 	eloop_cancel_timeout(auth_sae_process_commit, hapd, NULL);
 #endif /* CONFIG_SAE */
-
-#ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211AX
-	eloop_cancel_timeout(hostapd_switch_color_timeout_handler, hapd, NULL);
-
-#endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211AX */
 }
 
 
